# ── Ontology header ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/guides>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow> ;
    rdfs:comment """The pedagogy and adoption-guides slice: it dogfoods the curated recipes and learning paths that were formerly hardcoded in the documentation tooling, modelling them as gmeow:Recipe and gmeow:LearningPath individuals so they are authored-once GMEOW data sourced through the slice catalog rather than literals embedded in a Python module.

DOCTRINE.
  * Curated pedagogy, not domain axioms: a Recipe / LearningPath sequences EXISTING examples and terms for a developer adopting GMEOW; nothing here asserts a fact about the modelled world. The guides layer is pure documentation structure.
  * By reference (Principle 5): a guide names the example files and follow-on pages it builds on by slice-relative / documentation-relative PATH STRINGS and points at vocabulary terms by IRI; it never copies their content.
  * Authored once (Principle 4): each recipe and path is authored here once and projected outward by the documentation renderer into the recipes/, learning-paths/, and four-boxes/ pages, replacing the retired hardcoded tooling defaults."""@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/guides> ;
    rdfs:label "GMEOW Guides Module"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The GMEOW Guides Module — task-oriented adoption recipes (gmeow:Recipe) and curated learning paths (gmeow:LearningPath) that sequence canonical examples, vocabulary terms, and follow-on reading for a developer adopting GMEOW, dogfooded as authored-once GMEOW individuals."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxConfigBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox .
